WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.731
If an agent process disappears, task state

00:00:03.731 --> 00:00:06.928
should not disappear with it. Herdr

00:00:06.928 --> 00:00:09.060
Orchestrator places multiple coding

00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:12.258
harnesses behind one local control plane.

00:00:12.258 --> 00:00:15.455
Models may propose tasks and select

00:00:15.455 --> 00:00:19.186
workers. But Python and SQLite always own

00:00:19.186 --> 00:00:22.384
the queue, leases, retries, and success

00:00:22.384 --> 00:00:25.581
decisions. Remember it this way: Herdr

00:00:25.581 --> 00:00:28.246
hosts terminals, while the Coordinator

00:00:28.246 --> 00:00:29.845
owns the facts.

00:00:30.295 --> 00:00:34.033
The first step is loading a declarative

00:00:34.033 --> 00:00:37.771
workflow, not starting a model. TOML fixes

00:00:37.771 --> 00:00:39.908
concurrency, leases, timeouts, placement,

00:00:39.908 --> 00:00:43.646
and the allowed workers. The router sees

00:00:43.646 --> 00:00:47.384
only a compact harness catalog, not six

00:00:47.384 --> 00:00:50.588
long contexts. After Droid, Grok, Codex,

00:00:50.588 --> 00:00:54.326
Pi, Claude, or Hermes is selected, its

00:00:54.326 --> 00:00:58.065
full profile is injected at dispatch. This

00:00:58.065 --> 00:01:01.803
keeps context small and locks routing to

00:01:01.803 --> 00:01:02.871
configured candidates.

00:01:03.321 --> 00:01:07.217
After a task enters SQLite, its dedupe

00:01:07.217 --> 00:01:10.557
key prevents duplicate work. Claim runs

00:01:10.557 --> 00:01:13.897
inside an immediate write transaction. It

00:01:13.897 --> 00:01:17.237
increments the attempt, sets the lease,

00:01:17.237 --> 00:01:21.133
chooses a replica slot, and creates a

00:01:21.133 --> 00:01:25.030
correlation ID. Each wave claims only the

00:01:25.030 --> 00:01:27.256
configured capacity before dispatching

00:01:27.256 --> 00:01:29.483
through Herdr. Store deterministically

00:01:29.483 --> 00:01:32.266
folds outcomes into success, blocked,

00:01:32.266 --> 00:01:36.162
retry, or failure. A stale attempt can

00:01:36.162 --> 00:01:39.502
never overwrite a newly claimed execution.

00:01:39.952 --> 00:01:43.455
Herdr runtime does not treat a running

00:01:43.455 --> 00:01:46.958
process as proof that a task started.

00:01:46.958 --> 00:01:50.461
It first proves the pane shell is

00:01:50.461 --> 00:01:53.463
ready, then proves the harness is

00:01:53.463 --> 00:01:55.965
interactive. Before submitting the prompt,

00:01:55.965 --> 00:01:59.468
it records the state change sequence. Only

00:01:59.468 --> 00:02:02.971
a strict sequence advance proves a new

00:02:02.971 --> 00:02:06.474
turn. The turn must then stabilize in

00:02:06.474 --> 00:02:09.476
idle or done. Blocked, working, unknown,

00:02:09.476 --> 00:02:12.979
and timeout are not success. Every wait

00:02:12.979 --> 00:02:14.981
shares one bounded deadline.

00:02:15.431 --> 00:02:18.487
After choosing a worker, the system

00:02:18.487 --> 00:02:22.052
chooses where the task runs. A tab

00:02:22.052 --> 00:02:24.599
provides a dedicated visible location.

00:02:24.599 --> 00:02:28.164
Pane placement shares a tab within one

00:02:28.164 --> 00:02:30.711
wave while preserving separate terminals.

00:02:30.711 --> 00:02:33.767
Worktree placement creates a task branch,

00:02:33.767 --> 00:02:36.823
checkout, and Herdr workspace for write

00:02:36.823 --> 00:02:39.370
work. Explicit overrides and worker

00:02:39.370 --> 00:02:41.916
defaults come first. Deterministic read

00:02:41.916 --> 00:02:44.972
and write signals come next. Only

00:02:44.972 --> 00:02:48.028
ambiguous cases reach a bounded topology

00:02:48.028 --> 00:02:50.575
controller. A worktree isolates a

00:02:50.575 --> 00:02:52.103
checkout, not security.

00:02:52.553 --> 00:02:56.328
Each of the six harnesses receives fixed

00:02:56.328 --> 00:02:59.025
maximum automation flags that planners

00:02:59.025 --> 00:03:02.261
cannot override. These flags reduce local

00:03:02.261 --> 00:03:05.497
confirmations, but they do not authorize

00:03:05.497 --> 00:03:08.194
pushes, merges, publishing, or production

00:03:08.194 --> 00:03:10.890
actions. Claude workspace trust has

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:14.126
another guard. Three stable markers must

00:03:14.126 --> 00:03:17.362
appear, and the resolved execution root

00:03:17.362 --> 00:03:21.137
must match one complete output line. Login

00:03:21.137 --> 00:03:22.755
prompts, authentication, another

00:03:22.755 --> 00:03:25.452
directory, or missing markers never

00:03:25.452 --> 00:03:27.070
trigger automatic input.

00:03:27.520 --> 00:03:31.047
Settled only means the agent stopped. It

00:03:31.047 --> 00:03:34.574
does not prove the task is correct.

00:03:34.574 --> 00:03:38.101
An output receipt must appear in new

00:03:38.101 --> 00:03:41.628
lines from the current turn. Prompt echoes

00:03:41.628 --> 00:03:45.155
and old output cannot count. A file

00:03:45.155 --> 00:03:48.178
receipt must stay inside the execution

00:03:48.178 --> 00:03:50.697
root, reject absolute paths, parent

00:03:50.697 --> 00:03:53.217
traversal, and symlinks, and change

00:03:53.217 --> 00:03:56.744
relative to its baseline. Failed tasks may

00:03:56.744 --> 00:03:59.767
receive more attempt budget. Blocked tasks

00:03:59.767 --> 00:04:03.294
continue on the same agent, pane, and

00:04:03.294 --> 00:04:05.813
attempt after a reviewed response.

00:04:06.263 --> 00:04:08.855
The Dashboard projects SQLite durable

00:04:08.855 --> 00:04:13.001
state and Herdr runtime into one read-only

00:04:13.001 --> 00:04:16.111
snapshot. It shows queue state, attention

00:04:16.111 --> 00:04:19.221
items, receipt history, and a compound

00:04:19.221 --> 00:04:22.331
project, worktree, tab, and pane topology.

00:04:22.331 --> 00:04:24.922
Structural changes trigger layout, while

00:04:24.922 --> 00:04:28.032
status changes update content only, so

00:04:28.032 --> 00:04:31.142
live refreshes remain stable. The server

00:04:31.142 --> 00:04:34.770
binds only to loopback, validates Host and

00:04:34.770 --> 00:04:37.880
port, applies CSP and field allowlists,

00:04:37.880 --> 00:04:40.471
and never reads prompts, environment

00:04:40.471 --> 00:04:43.063
variables, or complete terminal output.

00:04:43.513 --> 00:04:45.575
Alongside ordinary dispatch, standardized

00:04:45.575 --> 00:04:48.152
delivery is available only through

00:04:48.152 --> 00:04:50.729
explicit opt-in. It resolves

00:04:50.729 --> 00:04:52.790
specification-blocking decisions, then

00:04:52.790 --> 00:04:55.367
creates an accepted spec and

00:04:55.367 --> 00:04:57.944
dependency-ordered ticket graph. Each

00:04:57.944 --> 00:05:01.037
ticket is implemented in an isolated

00:05:01.037 --> 00:05:04.129
worktree and closed with commit and

00:05:04.129 --> 00:05:06.191
acceptance evidence. After integration,

00:05:06.191 --> 00:05:09.799
fresh Standards and Spec reviewers run in

00:05:09.799 --> 00:05:12.376
parallel, and the controller adjudicates

00:05:12.376 --> 00:05:15.468
every finding. Repair rounds are bounded.

00:05:15.468 --> 00:05:18.561
Success stops on an isolated integration

00:05:18.561 --> 00:05:19.076
branch.

00:05:19.526 --> 00:05:23.136
This project is not an operating system

00:05:23.136 --> 00:05:25.715
sandbox. It protects state transitions,

00:05:25.715 --> 00:05:27.778
evidence, and authorization boundaries.

00:05:27.778 --> 00:05:30.872
Model artifacts pass exact-key, enum,

00:05:30.872 --> 00:05:33.451
length, and allowlist checks. Telemetry

00:05:33.451 --> 00:05:37.061
stays local by default, exporters are off

00:05:37.061 --> 00:05:40.156
by default, and fields are sanitized

00:05:40.156 --> 00:05:42.734
before persistence. The installer manages

00:05:42.734 --> 00:05:45.829
only manifest-owned project paths and

00:05:45.829 --> 00:05:48.923
stops conservatively on symlinks or user

00:05:48.923 --> 00:05:52.018
changes. Garbage collection starts as a

00:05:52.018 --> 00:05:55.112
dry run and requires creation, pane

00:05:55.112 --> 00:05:57.691
identity, and current ownership evidence.

00:05:58.141 --> 00:06:01.645
The Python control plane and npm wrapper

00:06:01.645 --> 00:06:04.648
have no third-party runtime package

00:06:04.648 --> 00:06:06.650
dependencies. External capabilities come

00:06:06.650 --> 00:06:10.154
from local command-line tools. The npm

00:06:10.154 --> 00:06:12.657
installer places workflows, profiles, and

00:06:12.657 --> 00:06:15.660
an ownership manifest into the target

00:06:15.660 --> 00:06:18.162
project while preserving user edits.

00:06:18.162 --> 00:06:20.665
Publishing starts after the complete

00:06:20.665 --> 00:06:24.169
quality gate on main. A dedicated runner

00:06:24.169 --> 00:06:27.673
only checks whether the registry lacks the

00:06:27.673 --> 00:06:31.176
version. The actual npm publish uses OIDC

00:06:31.176 --> 00:06:34.180
Trusted Publishing on a GitHub-hosted

00:06:34.180 --> 00:06:37.183
runner, without long-lived tokens or

00:06:37.183 --> 00:06:38.184
production deployment.

00:06:38.634 --> 00:06:41.235
The repository currently has nineteen

00:06:41.235 --> 00:06:43.835
reachable commits, twenty-six package

00:06:43.835 --> 00:06:46.436
Python modules, and one hundred

00:06:46.436 --> 00:06:49.037
ninety-eight static test functions.

00:06:49.037 --> 00:06:52.678
Physical test lines are about zero point

00:06:52.678 --> 00:06:56.319
eight eight to one compared with Python

00:06:56.319 --> 00:06:58.920
source. Contributors run focused tests

00:06:58.920 --> 00:07:02.561
first, then just check, followed by a

00:07:02.561 --> 00:07:06.202
real doctor or read-only smoke when

00:07:06.202 --> 00:07:08.802
needed. Remember three invariants: model

00:07:08.802 --> 00:07:11.403
output is constrained, the Coordinator

00:07:11.403 --> 00:07:14.524
owns state, and current execution must

00:07:14.524 --> 00:07:17.645
produce new evidence before success is

00:07:17.645 --> 00:07:18.165
accepted.
